{
  "summary": "The RNA-only, multiprofile PCA_n2000 model with transformer aggregation achieved validation accuracy 0.5191 and F1 0.4797, below the otherwise identical avgpool result of 0.5907 accuracy and 0.5727 F1, and below the multiprofile scVI_n200 avgpool/transformer results near 0.65 accuracy. This suggests that, for this PCA RNA representation, transformer aggregation did not reproduce the stronger multiprofile performance seen with avgpool or scVI, while still exceeding the single-profile PCA baseline of 0.4849 accuracy. It remains uncertain whether the lower result reflects transformer aggregation specifically, the PCA representation, or uncontrolled variability, so this should be treated as an initial observation rather than a definitive encoder/aggregation ranking."
}

